/* sql.Table ( qualifiedFieldName )
   Extracts the table-occurrence name from a GetFieldName result,
   then resolves the base table name via FileMaker_Tables.
   Returns the base table name for use in ExecuteSQL FROM clauses.

   Usage:
     "SELECT ... FROM " & sql.Table ( GetFieldName ( PEOPLE::PrimaryKey ) )

   Resolution path:
     1. GetFieldName ( TO::Field ) returns "TOName::FieldName"
     2. This function extracts "TOName"
     3. Looks up BaseTableName from FileMaker_Tables where TableName = TOName
     4. Returns the base table name, which is what ExecuteSQL needs

   FileMaker_Tables is a system virtual table available since FileMaker 12.
   It maps every table occurrence to its base table name and source file.
   This is NOT FileMaker_BaseTables, which requires FileMaker 2023 (20.1).

   If the TO cannot be resolved, returns "?" so the ExecuteSQL fails
   visibly (error 4413) rather than silently returning empty.

   Safety:
     A renamed base table: FileMaker_Tables reflects the new name immediately.
     A deleted TO: GetFieldName at the call site shows <Field Missing>.
     A renamed TO: FileMaker tracks the reference by id; GetFieldName
       returns the current name; this function resolves it.

   Performance:
     One ExecuteSQL call against a system table per invocation.
     Cache in a $ variable at script top when the same table
     appears in multiple queries within one script.

   Verify on first install:
     Confirm FileMaker_Tables.BaseTableName resolves on your version.
     Test: ExecuteSQL ( "SELECT BaseTableName FROM FileMaker_Tables
       WHERE TableName = 'PEOPLE'" ; "" ; "" ) should return "PEOPLE".
     If it returns "?" or errors, the column is not available and
     this function needs a fallback path through FileMaker_BaseTableFields.

   Requires: FileMaker 19 or later. No dependencies beyond sql.Field
   (conceptually paired, not called). */

Let (
    [
        _pos = Position ( qualifiedFieldName ; "::" ; 1 ; 1 ) ;
        _toName = If ( _pos > 0 ;
            Left ( qualifiedFieldName ; _pos - 1 ) ;
            qualifiedFieldName
        ) ;
        _baseTable = ExecuteSQL (
            "SELECT BaseTableName FROM FileMaker_Tables WHERE TableName = ?" ;
            "" ; "" ; _toName
        )
    ] ;
    If ( IsEmpty ( _baseTable ) or _baseTable = "?" ;
        "?" ;
        _baseTable
    )
)
